  "subject": "Candidate WVB 1.40 direct Vector parameter-length reads",
  "claim": "The current-source compiler emits the same 2,403-byte candidate module on Windows and Debian. Direct reads of empty and nonempty Vectors work through by-value, immutable and exclusive parameters; a later ownership transfer remains valid. Eleven malformed mutations reject at complete-verifier and runner boundaries, including read-after-move and wrong call mode; two invalid ownership sources reject during WIR validation. Existing owned-payload and borrow-runtime regressions pass on both hosts.",
  "source": {
    "kind": "Other",
    "value": "Worktree based on 46cfa827760721c7321fed9cb6c3f99c22798077, with exact changed implementation/test identities below. Authenticated predecessor analyzer and Emitter-Indexed-Budgets constructed candidate tool WVBs. Native packaging includes complete WVB verification. Debian executables package the Windows-produced native images; this is paired-host execution, not independent compiler reconstruction."
  },
